UID:bfc41ed90e3f7d4300c4023a9a9b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Music\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Emory Choirs and the Schwartz Center for Performi
 ng Arts\, this beloved candlelit choral concert returns to Glenn Auditoriu
 m at Glenn Memorial United Methodist Church for three concerts: Friday\, D
 ecember 4\, at 8 p.m.\, and Saturday\, December 5\, at 4 and 8 p.m.Under t
 he direction of Dr. Eric Nelson\, Emory professor of music and director of
  choral studies\, the program brings together the Emory Concert Choir and 
 University Chorus\, with special guests from the Emory community sharing s
 cripture readings that tell the Christmas story. Nelson has led the choirs
  in this Emory tradition for more than 25 years and this choral Christmas 
 service has been an Emory tradition since 1935. *Please\nCategory: Music\n
 Original listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/a-festival-of-nine-lessons
 -and-carols-2/2026-12-05/2/
LOCATION:Glenn Memorial United Methodist Church\, 1660 North Decatur Road
 \, Atlanta\, GA\, 30307
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/a-festival-of-nine-lessons-and-carols-2/
 2026-12-05/2/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
